WEBVTT

00:14.540 --> 00:16.440
May I talk now?

01:57.980 --> 02:00.080
I think I'll come along.

02:00.860 --> 02:02.020
Where to?

02:02.350 --> 02:03.970
The camping trip.

02:04.530 --> 02:06.780
Don't you need to teach?

02:07.290 --> 02:09.470
It's just one class in the afternoon.

02:09.470 --> 02:12.490
No, I don't think you should miss that.

02:13.030 --> 02:18.760
It's to practice living alone 
out in the wild, after all.

02:18.760 --> 02:22.120
It would defeat the purpose
 for me if you were there.

02:22.400 --> 02:25.650
I'll keep myself hidden, 
and I won't interfere.

02:25.950 --> 02:29.260
I might depend on you if 
I knew you were there.

02:29.770 --> 02:31.820
I won't put myself in danger.

02:32.330 --> 02:33.050
Okay?

02:35.830 --> 02:38.740
In other words, I just have to 
make sure I'm not useful to you.

02:47.780 --> 02:50.500
<i>I never would have thought 
he could duplicate himself.</i>

02:51.610 --> 02:56.460
<i>I don't do this often, so I can't share my 
vision or any other senses concurrently,</i>

02:56.460 --> 02:59.080
<i>but once I'm in one piece, 
they'll be shared.</i>

02:59.080 --> 03:03.540
<i>I'm not quite my full self without 
the other piece, so I'll stay at home.</i>

03:04.830 --> 03:06.700
<i>Or so he says.</i>

03:08.330 --> 03:09.230
Chise.

03:09.910 --> 03:11.930
I caught some fish from the river.

03:14.050 --> 03:15.540
<i>Oh well, I guess.</i>

03:23.300 --> 03:27.530
There's a lot of neighbors 
here... good neighbors.

03:28.140 --> 03:29.500
You're right.

03:29.500 --> 03:35.710
There are still a lot of old stories about 
them from Scotland and northern England.

03:37.040 --> 03:40.690
They must have had a deep 
relationship with humans.

03:42.680 --> 03:44.330
It's relaxing...

03:46.740 --> 03:50.900
<i>But I can't help but be a bit anxious.</i>

03:50.900 --> 03:51.530
Chise!

03:56.020 --> 03:58.330
Haven't you got enough yet?

03:58.330 --> 03:59.420
Start the fire already.

04:01.450 --> 04:03.050
Okay, got it.

04:03.580 --> 04:06.300
April, could you hammer that peg over there?

04:06.300 --> 04:07.400
Okay.

04:09.130 --> 04:12.240
Like this, and...

04:18.010 --> 04:19.930
I can't get it to work.

04:19.930 --> 04:21.860
You have to be quicker.

04:22.650 --> 04:25.060
Shave off some more to be sure.

04:26.620 --> 04:29.080
And start some good sparks.

04:33.140 --> 04:34.860
You're amazing.

04:34.860 --> 04:37.390
Could you teach me again tomorrow?

04:37.390 --> 04:38.700
I don't mind.

04:39.150 --> 04:41.740
I'll go get some water.

04:52.160 --> 04:53.220
<i>A horse?</i>

04:57.740 --> 04:58.770
<i>No.</i>

04:58.770 --> 05:00.160
<i>That's a fairy, too.</i>

05:00.620 --> 05:02.650
That's a kelpie.

05:02.650 --> 05:05.130
Or, no... it might be an each-uisge.

05:05.510 --> 05:06.900
An each-uisge?

05:07.530 --> 05:08.580
Yeah.

05:08.580 --> 05:12.590
They take reckless travelers 
and farmers on their backs.

05:12.590 --> 05:15.910
Then they run into water, 
drown them, and eat them.

05:16.720 --> 05:19.190
So don't get on its back.

05:20.580 --> 05:21.990
I'm not getting on.

05:25.510 --> 05:26.530
The river...

05:27.530 --> 05:30.540
I'll be at the lake ahead of the river.

05:38.770 --> 05:40.360
That took you a while.

05:40.360 --> 05:44.370
Lucy, if you see a horse out
 there, don't get on, okay?

05:44.370 --> 05:45.220
A horse?

05:50.600 --> 05:52.700
It's getting dark.

05:54.890 --> 05:57.760
<i>Her eyes don't look like human eyes.</i>

05:58.480 --> 06:02.210
<i>Are mages all like this?</i>

06:29.230 --> 06:34.180
<i>I can't tell if those are voices of 
other students or of the neighbors.</i>

06:36.790 --> 06:38.750
Ruth and I are both here.

06:38.750 --> 06:39.410
Hey.

06:40.000 --> 06:43.340
This is supposed to be a practical for me.

07:00.640 --> 07:02.960
<i>Ah, well.</i>

07:20.900 --> 07:22.760
The birds are so loud.

07:35.780 --> 07:36.990
Morning.

07:37.480 --> 07:38.850
Morning.

07:38.850 --> 07:40.260
You're up early.

07:41.400 --> 07:43.540
I always am.

07:43.540 --> 07:44.680
Ah.

07:45.710 --> 07:46.470
Bye.

07:59.190 --> 08:02.620
<i>She's still hanging onto that potpourri.</i>

08:03.640 --> 08:06.900
Why do you care about her?

08:06.900 --> 08:07.810
Who?

08:09.270 --> 08:10.790
I'm talking about Sergeant.

08:11.640 --> 08:13.210
I don't know.

08:14.470 --> 08:16.000
You don't have a reason?

08:17.050 --> 08:21.260
It's not exactly that she's relatable...

08:24.560 --> 08:27.320
But I think she could talk more.

08:28.120 --> 08:29.380
What about you?

08:29.380 --> 08:30.750
What about me?

08:30.750 --> 08:32.850
You seem to hate Philomela.

08:33.320 --> 08:34.570
Is that a bad thing?

08:34.800 --> 08:36.020
No.

08:36.020 --> 08:38.210
I just wonder if there's a reason.

08:38.720 --> 08:43.150
I hate sorcerers.

08:44.270 --> 08:46.110
Why are you at the College, then?

08:50.290 --> 08:51.660
The fire's out.

08:52.140 --> 08:53.720
While I wash my face,

08:53.720 --> 08:56.380
can you set things up to reignite it?

08:56.380 --> 08:57.100
Okay.

09:43.810 --> 09:46.270
I guess we're going home tomorrow.

09:46.270 --> 09:47.150
Yeah.

09:48.420 --> 09:50.510
That felt like an instant.

09:52.430 --> 09:55.070
I have to study as soon as I get home.

09:56.060 --> 09:57.590
Do you like studying?

09:59.870 --> 10:03.270
There's a lot I need to accomplish.

10:03.670 --> 10:05.130
Unlike you.

10:06.050 --> 10:09.630
There's something I need 
to do, too, actually.

10:10.550 --> 10:13.010
I don't know when I'll be done, though.

10:14.540 --> 10:15.560
Oh, yeah?

10:21.520 --> 10:22.800
What?

10:22.800 --> 10:24.850
Why don't you tell me what it is?!

10:28.810 --> 10:30.460
Good night, Lucy.

10:31.110 --> 10:32.190
Night.

10:45.670 --> 10:46.900
Bathroom.

11:17.790 --> 11:20.920
<i>Why is my skin prickling?</i>

11:21.790 --> 11:22.970
Are you up?

11:22.970 --> 11:24.520
I feel that disturbance, too.

11:25.160 --> 11:26.490
Do you?

11:27.770 --> 11:28.860
Lucy!

11:30.280 --> 11:32.560
She's been gone for a while.

11:36.900 --> 11:37.990
Lucy!

11:37.990 --> 11:39.100
Lucy!

11:39.490 --> 11:40.820
Lucy?

11:46.330 --> 11:47.130
Lucy!

11:47.380 --> 11:48.670
What happened?

11:49.340 --> 11:51.600
Looks like her magic power is dried up.

11:52.850 --> 11:57.510
Magic power is as important to 
us as life is to normal people.

11:57.510 --> 11:59.230
She's in a bit of danger.

11:59.430 --> 12:02.230
Can we not share any with her?

12:02.560 --> 12:03.970
You could.

12:03.970 --> 12:06.230
You have far more than enough.

12:10.580 --> 12:12.200
Hold her close by.

12:12.980 --> 12:18.670
Since her power is dried up, 
she'll naturally suck up yours.

12:19.500 --> 12:23.810
Ruth, please tell Mr. Whoopi about this.

12:23.810 --> 12:24.960
Got it.

12:25.270 --> 12:27.590
We have to get back to the tent.

12:38.410 --> 12:43.810
<i>Since the day my arm changed, my senses 
have broadened even more than before.</i>

12:45.180 --> 12:48.320
<i>I can see the outlines of 
things I couldn't see before.</i>

12:48.990 --> 12:52.340
<i>Their movements, their whispers,</i>

12:52.810 --> 12:55.570
<i>their touch... all of it 
became easier to sense.</i>

12:57.970 --> 13:00.610
<i>So I'd let my guard down a bit.</i>

13:01.700 --> 13:05.420
<i>There's more in the darkness 
that I don't know about.</i>

13:06.600 --> 13:08.150
A centaur?

13:08.150 --> 13:10.220
No, that's not a centaur.

13:10.690 --> 13:14.440
It's a sea monster that brings 
calamity to island and highland alike.

13:14.440 --> 13:16.060
A nuckelavee.

13:16.620 --> 13:18.230
A nuckelavee...

13:21.550 --> 13:22.910
Chise, run!

13:23.260 --> 13:24.110
Where?

13:24.510 --> 13:26.600
That thing can't touch freshwater.

13:26.980 --> 13:28.040
Freshwater...

13:28.500 --> 13:29.570
The river!

13:33.750 --> 13:36.220
The magic power isn't flowing naturally.

13:36.620 --> 13:37.840
I need to look into this.

13:44.910 --> 13:47.160
Why is it attacking us?

13:47.360 --> 13:48.690
Who knows?

13:48.690 --> 13:52.730
Rumor has it that it can't help 
but kill humans on sight.

13:53.460 --> 13:56.520
It also wrecks crops by spewing poison mist.

13:57.200 --> 14:00.210
Maybe it left the sea because 
nothing's come along in a while

14:00.210 --> 14:02.230
that can see it like we can.

14:02.460 --> 14:05.350
Then did the nuckelavee get Lucy?

14:05.350 --> 14:08.550
I don't think so. That's 
not the way it attacks.

14:08.550 --> 14:10.520
Chise! Elias!

14:10.520 --> 14:11.400
Ruth!

14:11.910 --> 14:13.200
Where's the teacher?

14:13.200 --> 14:14.490
Couldn't find him.

14:15.150 --> 14:17.260
I did come across these guys, though.

14:17.810 --> 14:19.220
Is something wrong with Lucy?

14:20.130 --> 14:21.170
Everyone, run!

14:29.260 --> 14:30.050
Zoe!

14:45.470 --> 14:46.730
It stopped.

14:47.500 --> 14:48.950
You did it, Zoe!

14:52.750 --> 14:53.650
Zoe!

15:04.950 --> 15:06.380
Poison mist!

15:06.380 --> 15:08.500
Everyone, get to the 
other side of the river!

15:23.240 --> 15:25.450
What do we do, Elias?

15:25.910 --> 15:28.360
There's nothing I can do in my state.

15:28.830 --> 15:32.360
My original self could eat it, 
destroy it, or what have you.

15:32.360 --> 15:36.380
But as you wished, this 
me can't do anything.

15:36.890 --> 15:39.550
You're training yourself on how
 not to rely on me, aren't you?

15:43.910 --> 15:45.890
I need advice, Elias.

15:46.340 --> 15:54.390
Do you think the fairy and the lake
 past the river from yesterday would help?

15:58.310 --> 16:00.250
I don't mind giving you advice.

16:02.110 --> 16:05.000
That one would definitely 
make for a good ride.

16:09.720 --> 16:11.830
Come. Come.

16:13.550 --> 16:15.040
I shall ask for you.

16:15.500 --> 16:16.830
I shall beg for you.

16:18.030 --> 16:21.160
Come here, horse of the water.

16:23.790 --> 16:26.340
I see. You want a ride.

16:26.340 --> 16:29.730
Could you draw that thing towards the lake?

16:30.590 --> 16:33.160
Very well. Very well.

16:33.540 --> 16:34.570
Get on.

16:35.350 --> 16:36.380
Get on.

16:37.080 --> 16:38.030
Get on.

16:38.880 --> 16:41.010
Ruth, take Lucy.

16:42.720 --> 16:43.500
All right.

16:48.050 --> 16:48.860
Chise.

16:49.190 --> 16:50.350
I'm coming with you.

16:50.350 --> 16:51.780
It's dangerous.

16:51.780 --> 16:54.000
It's even more dangerous 
for you to go alone.

16:54.350 --> 16:56.060
Rian, here!

16:59.830 --> 17:00.760
Appreciate it!

17:09.860 --> 17:11.150
It's coming.

17:16.130 --> 17:21.190
I envy you, being able to run off 
without looking back, Rian.

17:22.760 --> 17:25.070
My, what are you lot doing out here?

17:25.070 --> 17:27.060
Sir, we have a problem!

17:31.480 --> 17:33.750
It hates fresh water.

17:33.750 --> 17:36.240
So if we lure it to the 
lake and dunk it in...

17:36.240 --> 17:38.000
It might run away.

17:38.540 --> 17:42.370
But each-uisge eat humans in the water.

17:43.080 --> 17:46.250
So you need to get back to 
shore as quickly as you can.

18:28.070 --> 18:30.860
Fresh water is poisonous to it.

18:30.860 --> 18:31.740
Chise!

18:31.740 --> 18:32.790
Let's get ashore.

18:32.790 --> 18:33.520
Right.

18:42.530 --> 18:44.650
You perceive...

18:45.530 --> 18:47.650
You recognize...

18:48.230 --> 18:50.650
You see behind the shadow...

18:50.990 --> 18:52.500
And I will not spare you.

18:53.760 --> 18:58.870
So long as you look into 
our side, we will...

18:59.380 --> 19:00.560
<i>Horror.</i>

19:00.840 --> 19:02.220
<i>It must be destroyed.</i>

19:04.470 --> 19:07.230
<i>Horrors must be destroyed.</i>

19:36.600 --> 19:39.760
You got out of the water.

19:39.760 --> 19:44.650
I'll have to eat the one 
still in the water instead.

19:50.860 --> 19:51.960
You will not.

19:54.970 --> 19:56.220
Metal...

19:56.420 --> 20:00.840
<i>You never let me down, Isaac.</i>

20:02.260 --> 20:07.350
I'm not good at using sorcery on others, 
but I'm good at using it on myself.

20:09.650 --> 20:10.640
Chise!

20:11.120 --> 20:12.640
Rian.

20:12.640 --> 20:13.640
Are you all right?

20:13.930 --> 20:15.640
Yeah, I'm fine.

20:16.490 --> 20:18.730
I can't eat you now.

20:22.310 --> 20:24.420
Where's Elias?

20:28.810 --> 20:31.710
Oh, yeah, why are you here, sir?

20:35.550 --> 20:36.740
I'm dry.

20:45.340 --> 20:47.890
<i>Just what was that?</i>

20:48.580 --> 20:52.820
<i>I would have died instead if 
I hadn't done what I did.</i>

20:53.360 --> 20:54.230
<i>But...</i>

20:55.650 --> 20:59.040
<i>I still feel it.</i>

21:06.750 --> 21:07.960
Um...

21:07.960 --> 21:10.680
I can't give you my flesh, but...

21:12.370 --> 21:13.200
Ack.

21:22.480 --> 21:26.360
No more drunkards at night.

21:26.360 --> 21:28.490
No more night travelers.

21:28.490 --> 21:30.140
No one standing around.

21:30.470 --> 21:34.320
No one has walked the night in a while.

21:34.320 --> 21:36.640
How disappointing not to eat you.

21:40.920 --> 21:42.170
Shall we get going?

21:42.790 --> 21:44.020
We should.

21:52.890 --> 21:54.120
Are you okay?

21:54.120 --> 21:55.270
Okay how?

21:55.270 --> 21:58.050
I've seen that face before.

22:00.960 --> 22:02.230
In the mirror.

22:12.640 --> 22:16.600
I didn't know what to do.

22:17.980 --> 22:19.100
Yeah.
